      "text": "Modular curves, invariant theory and E 8 — The E8 root lattice can be constructed from the modular curve X(13) by the invariant theory for the simple group PSL(2, 13).\n\n**Modular curves, invariant theory and E 8**\n\n*Lei Yang*\n\n39 pp, 13 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** The E8 root lattice can be constructed from the modular curve X(13) by the invariant theory for the simple group PSL(2, 13). This gives a diﬀerent construction of the E8 root lattice. It also gives an explicit construction of the modular curve X(13).\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Abstract; Contents; 1 Introduction; 2 Standard construction: from the icosahedron ; 2.1 E8-singularity: from the icosahedron to E8; 2.2 The Barlow surface: from the icosahedron t; 2.3 Bring’s curve and Fricke’s octavic curve: ; 3 Modular curve X(13) and invariant theory for; 4 A diﬀerent construction: from the modular cu; 4.3 Bring’s curve and Fricke’s octavic curve: ; 5 An explicit construction of the modular curv; References",
